    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP, today\u2019s slate centers on high-upside speed threats and favorable matchups against soft-tossing righties. **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 82.07 score; despite facing a modest hold-percentage threat from the opposition\u2019s battery, his premium placement in the third spot against the highly hittable M\u00e1rquez (5.64 xERA) makes him our top option. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90) benefits from a massive 16% park factor boost and a slow pitcher delivery that signals a high stolen base probability, while **James Wood** (72.06) rounds out our primary tier. The combination of **Wood**'s 0.424 xwOBA and his prime leadoff position against Imai puts him in a position to anchor our Runs and SB categories today.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Max Muncy**, who finished just outside the starting rotation with a 43.15 score. While **Muncy** typically provides reliable power, his matchup against the elite arm of Skubal (2.74 xERA) creates a significant SP skill penalty that suppressed his efficiency, ultimately forcing him to the bench in favor of more favorable platoon matchups like **Kyle Karros** (61.16). **Karros** is a strategic start today, as he faces a left-hander where his platoon advantage, combined with a slow pitcher delivery that invites aggression on the basepaths, creates a high-ceiling opportunity.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the volatility of the league's scarcity-driven landscape. We are keeping a close eye on **Jose Caballero** and **Mickey Moniak**, both of whom face potential turbulence in their lineups; while **Caballero** maintains a strong dynamic platoon edge (13%), his low park factor limits his ceiling. Managers should note that while we have avoided high-risk exposures like **Austin Riley** against Skenes or **Henry Bolte** against Skubal, the high scores for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Dalton Rushing** suggest we are well-positioned to capitalize on our targets' favorable xERA matchups. Remain disciplined with your daily game caps as we look to extend our lead in speed-dependent categories.",
